# tests/proof_patch_test.tg — third-audit items 29 (the first-class evidence
# deltas: SourceDelta / DropPlanDelta / ObligationResults / AllocationDelta /
# CoverageDelta / PerformanceDelta / EquivalenceResult) and 32 (the
# refactor-equivalence gate) end-to-end lane.
#
# The model itself lives in tg_compiler/proof_patch.tg (ProofCarryingPatch,
# PatchEvidenceBundle, SourceDelta, AllocationDelta, proof_patch_of_delta /
# proof_patch_between, proof_patch_lane_check) with the §36 gate in
# tg_compiler/change_budget.tg (EquivalenceRequirement,
# budget_verify_with_equivalence, budget_refactor_default /
# budget_refactor_with_level) and the gating ladder in
# tg_compiler/equivalence.tg (equivalence_level_rank,
# equivalence_result_satisfies). This test drives the self-checking lane
# rows:
#   proof_patch_lane_check — P1 the claim-nothing patch defaults every new
#     evidence surface empty; P2 the delta-derived alloc-class row and the
#     sink-bearing drop-plan row (the let/inout row emits nothing); P3 the
#     full evidence bundle is carried verbatim and the caller allocation
#     rows append; P4 the refactor budget reports the missing equivalence
#     result and a proven result clears it; P5/P6 TestedNoCounterexample
#     violates under the default proof demand and passes when the budget
#     does not demand a proof.
#
# The helper returns mismatch rows (empty = the whole lane verifies).
#
# Run with the repo root as the working directory:
#   tg test tests/proof_patch_test.tg

use std::test::assert

use tg_compiler::proof_patch::{proof_patch_lane_check}

@test
def test_proof_patch_evidence_deltas_and_equivalence_gate_lane() -> Unit
  let rows = proof_patch_lane_check()
  assert(rows.len() == 0, "proof patch lane mismatches: " + rows.join("; "))
end
